1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,048
How do you make sure a card is charged exactly once?

2
00:00:03,098 --> 00:00:10,848
At a bank's cash desk, only one cashier can hold the withdrawal slip, and the cashier writes it in the logbook before opening the drawer.

3
00:00:10,898 --> 00:00:12,720
The charge works the same way.

4
00:00:12,770 --> 00:00:19,080
First, one claim lets exactly one caller win, however many clicks or retries arrive.

5
00:00:19,130 --> 00:00:21,720
The winner finds the live terminal and the fee.

6
00:00:21,770 --> 00:00:25,464
Without either, the payment fails, and nothing is charged.

7
00:00:25,514 --> 00:00:29,784
Then it writes the charge in the logbook, before any network is asked.

8
00:00:29,834 --> 00:00:37,416
ecom asks the card zone to charge the card by its token, with an id that makes the charge happen once, even if it is sent twice.

9
00:00:37,466 --> 00:00:43,080
Some networks only hold the money at first; for those, the card zone takes it at once.

10
00:00:43,130 --> 00:00:44,952
Approved means paid.

11
00:00:45,002 --> 00:00:46,824
Declined is final.

12
00:00:46,874 --> 00:00:50,424
And no answer in time is unknown, never declined.

13
00:00:50,474 --> 00:00:53,520
Next: what happens when the network goes silent.
